  "summary": "After spending several years as a carpenter. I made the huge jump to web development in 2010. My attention to detail in carpentry stuck with me which plays out well in building and develping websites. Most days you can find me behind a computer writing clean code and building custom Wordpress themes for my clients. I love being able to build websites that a client can easily maintain after the project is finished. I also believe in doing things right the first time, so I follow a workflow that is advantagous for both myself and the client.\n\nTraverse City Web and WordPress Developer. Specializing in WordPress management, custom theme building, and eCommerce. I also have experience with Squarespace, Shopify, Hubspot, osCommerce, Twitter Bootstrap, Foundation and plenty more. I build mobile first, responsive websites.",
